  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ENFORCEMENT AND PROSECUTION: MAKING A CASE FOR THE MALAYAN TIGER</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO SECURE STRONG CONVICTION OUTCOMES FOR TIGERS AND OTHER WILDLIFE CRIMES, WHICH WILL HAVE A SECONDARY EFFECT OF PREVENTING THE CONTINUED LOSS OF THE MALAYAN TIGER POPULATION. THIS WILL BE ACHIEVED BY WORKING CLOSELY WITH THE DEPARTMENT OF WILDLIFE AND NATIONAL PARKS PENINSULAR MALAYSIA (DWNP) LEGAL AND ENFORCEMENT TEAMS (THE KEY BENEFICIARIES OF CAPACITY BUILDING), PUBLIC PROSECUTORS AND THE ROYAL MALAYSIAN POLICE TO ACHIEVE THE FOLLOWING THREE OBJECTIVES: (1) BY MONTH 36, AT LEAST 50% OF THE ENFORCEMENT TEAM TARGETED BY THE PROJECT SHOW IMPROVEMENT IN THEIR KNOWLEDGE AND PROFICIENCY TO INVESTIGATE CRIMES INVOLVING TIGERS AND THEIR PREY (2) BY MONTH 36, ACHIEVE AT LEAST 50% OF THE PROSECUTED TIGER AND OTHER TOTALLY PROTECTED WILDLIFE CASES TRIED BY DWNP LEAD TO A CONVICTION AND (3) BY MONTH 36, AT LEAST 50% OF CONVICTED CASES SEE PENALTIES IN ACCORDANCE TO THE WILDLIFE CRIME SENTENCING GUIDELINE PRODUCED UNDER THE PROJECT.</narrative>
  </description>
